@HansGrob Singapore has avoided war since it became independent.  While North and South Korea didn’t sign a peace treaty, the stand off has lasted since 1953 which gave time for South Korea to become a modern nation.  Ditto for Taiwan.  Of course, overnight conditions may change, just ask any Ukrainian !

Please note, I did not say avoiding world wars was the only reason but one reason.

One thing I’ll say for the Swiss, they seem to have avoided the economic suicide that countries like Australia seem bent on participating in.  Green hydrogen anyone?  Or planning on building an underground rail that goes from nowhere to nowhere and will almost certainly be abandoned costing billions of dollars.

@ladislavzima8382 Let me simplify it even more for you.  If you want to trade with the US, then you go by the US' trade rules.

Therefore, if we want to jack up our tariffs on Swiss products to 30% (or even 137%) like you do to our products, that's our rule.  If you don't like it, then simply don't trade with us.  We'll start buying our own JN Shapiro luxury watches instead of Rolexes.  See how simple that is?

BTW, shouldn't Americans be dying by the thousands if we're eating poisonous food?  Do you know what critical thinking is?
